==English==
{{was wotd|2009|September|13}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Korkenzieher 01 KMJ.jpg|thumb|A '''corkscrew''']]
From {{compound|cork|screw|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈkɔːk.skɹuː/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈkɔɹk.skɹu/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-corkscrew.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An implement for [[open]]ing [[bottles]] that are sealed by a [[cork]]. Sometimes specifically such an implement that includes a screw-shaped part, or [[worm]].
#: ''I opened the wine with a '''corkscrew'''.''
#* {{quote-book|1720|[[w:Nicholas Amhurst|Nicholas Amhurst]]|chapter=The Bottle-Scrue|Poems on Several Occasions|page=113|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=Uw8UAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA113
|passage=There stood presented to his sight, Or seem'd to stand, the God of wine, {{...}} This hand a '''''Cork-scrue''''' did contain, And that a Bottle of ''Champaign''.}}<!-- first known use -->
#* {{quote-journal|1999|James Lighthill|Biofluiddynamics: A Survey|Contemporary Mathematics|volume=141|page=11|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=nCvG2t02114C&pg=PA11
|passage=A '''corkscrew''' is designed so that when it is turned it creates effectively a helical undulation pushing it into the cork, whereas rotation in the opposite sense pulls it out.}}
#* {{quote-book|2006|Costas Katsigris & Chris Thomas|The Bar and Beverage Book|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=gtKOyU9ci1MC&pg=PA152|page=152|edition=4th ed.
|passage=A two-prong or ah-so '''corkscrew''' with sheath.}}
# The screw-shaped [[worm]] of a typical corkscrew.
#* {{quote-book|1898|[[w:Herbert Spencer|Herbert Spencer]]|First Principles of a New System of Philosophy|url=http://www.archive.org/details/firstprincipleso00spenrich
|passage=A bubble rising rapidly in water describes a spiral closely resembling a '''corkscrew'''.}}
# {{lb|en|boxing|martial arts}} A type of sharp, [[twisting]] [[punch]], often one thrown close and from the side.
#* {{quote-book|2002|Darin Strauss|The Real McCoy|page=42|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=w1JbAAAAMAAJ|isbn=0525946519
|passage={{...}} the immovable McCoy let fly his most miraculous punch of the evening, of his lives, a world-beater of a right '''corkscrew''', a punch years in the windup {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|amusement rides}} A type of [[inversion]] used in [[roller coaster]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|1987|September|Tim Cole|Killer Coasters|Popular Mechanics|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=zeQDAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA56|page=56
|passage=A '''corkscrew''' has a 90° turn just prior to the loop and a 90° turn just afterward.}}

